<ChartsRuntimeNotice />
<DocsExample TExample="LineInterpolationExample" Title="Interpolation" Description="Interpolation controls how the line connects points. Keep Straight for measured values, use Smoothed or Curved for trends, and use Step for values that hold until the next change, such as a price or a plan limit." />
<DocsExample TExample="LineStyleMarkersExample" Title="Dashed lines and point markers" Description="LineStyle, StrokeWidth, PointStyle and PointShape separate series that share a chart, which also helps readers who can't tell the colors apart. Use a dashed line for a forecast or a target." />
<DocsExample TExample="LineDataLabelsExample" Title="Data labels" Description="ShowDataLabels prints each value next to its point, and DataLabelFormat formats it. Use labels on short series where readers want exact numbers without hovering." />
<DocsExample TExample="LineTooltipExample" Title="Tooltips for overlapping points" Description="When points from several line, area or point series sit on top of each other, the tooltip lists all of them, in chart order. A point counts as overlapping when it is drawn within OverlapDistance (8dp by default) of the hovered point: try April, where the two lines nearly meet, at each distance. Set ShowAllSeriesAtX on NTTooltip to list every series that has a value at the hovered X, so readers can compare series without hunting for each point." />
<DocsExample TExample="LineLargeDataExample" Title="Large data set" Description="A series draws thousands of points without slowing the page. This chart plots 5,000 samples; zoom with the scroll wheel and drag to pan to inspect detail." />
<DocsExample TExample="LineDateGroupingExample" Title="Date grouping" Description="On a date axis, dense data is grouped by year or month as you zoom out. Select a group to zoom into it, and OnDateGroupClick reports the group that was selected." />
